# GitHub Copilot / IntelliCode Rules for EIRMS

## Project context

- Core stack: Next.js App Router, Supabase, Shadcn/ui (Radix + Tailwind) and Bun.
- Keep features compliant with EIRMS PRD, architecture and strict TypeScript patterns.
- Prefer server actions (Next.js form actions) and guarded access around Supabase auth.

## Shadcn component usage

- Use `@/components/ui/*` wrappers for UI primitives (`Button`, `Input`, `Label`, `Select`, `Textarea`, `Card`, `Dialog`, `Table`, `Tabs`, etc.).
- Do not duplicate component-level behavior; prefer composing existing shadcn variants and tokens.
- Keep `@/components/ui` wrappers aligned with shadcn naming and props conventions.
- Style with Tailwind classes, route all theme color adjustments through design tokens (e.g. `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`).

## Forms and accessibility

- For controlled `Select` / `Checkbox` code, keep `use client` on component files.
- For server components, avoid client-only Radix wrappers unless separated into client subcomponents.
- Keep semantic labels via `Label` and add `aria-*` accessibility attributes for form validation.

## Copilot prompt hygiene

- When generating code, avoid hardcoded magic strings; prefer types/enums for role values (e.g. `role: "end_user" | ...`).
- Preserve existing structure when refactoring pages; keep page-level data fetching and table columns intact.
- Do not introduce third-party UI libraries beyond shadcn (no MUI, Chakra, etc.).

## CI and VS Code

- Use linting from `bun run lint` and format via `bunx prettier --write .`.
- Keep VS Code settings for Copilot in workspace config (if present) consistent with this rule guidance.
